# Digests of the published componentize-js builds for the revision pinned in
# componentize-js.rev. The pin covers bytes, not just a filename: nothing
# else ties a downloaded toolchain to that revision, and the toolchain is the
# compiler that produces the wasm component the WPT gate tests — a tampered
# one can emit a backdoored component and a green run.
#
# One line per platform:
#
#     <platform>  <sha256 of the published .gz asset>  <sha256 of the binary>
#
# The asset digest is what the build-provenance attestation signs, and is
# checked on download. The binary digest is what actually gets executed, and
# is checked on every use, including from the local cache.
#
# Regenerate with `just update-toolchain-digest` when the revision changes:
# it verifies the attestation before recording, so adding a line here is the
# deliberate, reviewable act of trusting a new binary.
linux-x86_64  9954f2a66d5165ca86c425c297d6b7b98f8760c5e97cf910b9e0fc3afd23121d  bbf7be7397518def75f030821d759f15765bd13cdb20416e009c1e68bef64dc7
linux-aarch64  8ce76bd96feaf68fb2439f7b49d631adba7cdfc930442baf2eea77142d6d74c8  fe8b00ff3ca78ea99563bfdc1a7371fc7b839ede3070a7c9437d2b3858989ae1
